# API Layer (`apps/web/src/api`)

## Client

`base/client.ts` uses `fetch` with `credentials: 'include'`. It obtains an antiforgery token and adds `X-CSRF-TOKEN` to state-changing requests.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const user = parseUser(await httpClient.get<unknown>('/auth/me'))
```

## BaseApiService

```typescript
class ExampleApi extends BaseApiService<Example> {
  constructor() {
    super('example')
  }
}
export const exampleApi = new ExampleApi()
```

## Types / light validation

Define interfaces in `types/schema.ts`. Use small `parse*` helpers when runtime checks matter.

## Core APIs

| Client | Role |
|--------|------|
| `authApi.ts` | login/me/logout/profile/password |
| `usersApi.ts` | global user administration |
| `rolesApi.ts` | global roles and permission catalog |
| `securityAuditApi.ts` | security audit |
| `modules/*` | Explicitly registered product modules |

Paths are relative to `BASE_URL`, which normalizes to `/api/v1`. Always use the shared client so cookie and CSRF behavior remains consistent.
